      "message": "Rob: is there a better way to determine if a shader will use prior-stage output? AFAICS it\u0027s not a trivial problem to solve; we have to create a key just to inspect it. And unfortunately, we need to know the answer BEFORE inserting the shader into the key. (If we could create key portions out-of-order and then combine them, we could avoid doing the work twice.)\n\nOr: technically, we could just always emit the solid color, even if it\u0027s unused. It burns one half4 uniform in the case where we have a shader that ignores the prior-stage. (I tried this approach as well, and it broke some CombinationBuilder tests, but I wasn\u0027t sure how that code worked.)",
